{
  "abstract": "We construct a directed strongly regular graph on one hundred vertices with in-degree and out-degree 17, nine reciprocal neighbors at each vertex, and two or three directed walks of length two between distinct vertices according as the corresponding arc is present or absent. Its directed complement realizes the parameters (100,82,74,67,68). The construction takes twenty pentagons, prescribes cyclic matchings between their fibres by ten quadratic polynomials over the field of five elements, and admits a free cyclic automorphism of order five. We give the complete arc rule, a finite integer verification on relative displacements, and an independently checked adjacency matrix. The derivation uses two symmetric seven-regular layers and an invertible product on their forty-dimensional spaces of contrasts within fibres. Two explicit five-color partitions extend the example to a directed strongly regular graph with parameters (100m,20m−3,4m+5,4m−2,4m−1) for every positive integer m. Intrinsic neighborhood partitions recover the copies and give an exact isomorphism criterion for arbitrary color matchings between copies. Within this construction there are 300 uncolored isomorphism classes at order 200 and 3,981,347,520 at order 300.",
